---
title: Snowy owl
---
# Snowy owl

The snowy owl breeds on the arctic tundra, where the male is almost pure white
and the female heavily barred. Because the arctic summer has no darkness at all,
it forages in broad daylight there; farther south in winter it returns to
crepuscular habits. Lemmings dominate the diet, and breeding success follows the
lemming cycle so closely that a pair may not lay at all in a poor year. It nests
on a low rise on open ground, with no cover but the female's own vigilance. See
[[strigidae]].
